{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 32, :comments ["<b>Look, I am going to die.</b> (The birthright totters and goes — that the Temple service would not always be through the firstborns, for the tribe of Levi will take it, and furthermore) Esav said: What is the nature of this service? He said to him: How many warnings and punishments and death-penalties hang over it, like that which we learned: these are punishable by death — those who drink wine and those with dishevelled hair. He said: I am going to die through it — if so, what do I want with it?"], :book :genesis, :voice :rashi, :lang :en, :chapter 25, :notes {}, :source-witnesses nil, :timestamp "2026-08-02T09:00:32.384484266Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}